<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Elan says international division president to retire.</title>
<headline>Elan says international division president to retire.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish-based drug  company Elan Corporation Plc said on Wednesday that Kenneth McVey would retire as a director and as president of its international division with effect from the end of 1996.</p>
<p>McVey, who is 57, joined Elan in 1984 and was responsible for a number of areas including licensing, commercial development and intellectual property, Elan said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
